    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAnnacrivey comes to the market in turn-key condition. This Art Deco home has undergone a thorough refurbishment project carried out in 2019/2020 with impeccable attention to detail under the guidance of Kruger/Lyons Architects. Design details are sympathetic and consistent to its Art Deco origins enjoying an emphasis on modernity, symmetry, bold geometry and streamlined design. Boasting curved corners, strong geometric shapes, mix of chevron wood and terrazzo flooring along are complemented by decorative, clean lines to include horizontal glass brick detailing. \n\nQuality fixtures and fittings throughout ensure that this home presents as a fine ready to walk into home. Annacrivey is engraved in the terrazzo steps leading to the hall door. In turn the hall is welcoming reflecting light from the polished terrazzo flooring and glass brick detailing on the stair well. To the left is a generous sized and well-fitted study complete with desk unit, storage presses and shelving unit. To the right is the dining area complete with chevron flooring with soft uplighting, fitted sideboard with ample storage for delf and glasses. From here a door leads to the family room. This dual aspect room is the ideal snug area with a slightly more informal vibe.\n\nStriking Crittall-style doors opens from the hall to the living room. This spacious and bright room enjoys wall to wall windows overlooking the back garden with French doors to the patio. It features a delightful open marble fireplace with Art Deco detailing. \n\nThe kitchen is a delight. Three gentle steps ascend to this open bright area with centre island providing family-friendly dining space for bar stools and banquette seating for more formal dining occasions. The kitchen, by Noel Dempsey kitchens, enjoys every modern convenience in a very considered design. Storage solutions include a larder drawer with concertina doors, undercounter presses and wine cooler. The appliances are top of the range Siemens and include steam cooker and coffee maker. This is without doubt the hub of the house. \n\nThe adjoining utility room is equally well designed, featuring provision for waist level appliances, a sink unit and direct access to the side passage. A stylish guest toilet completes the ground floor accommodation. \n\nUpstairs the luxurious principal suite enjoys a dual-aspect orientation and comprises a beautifully appointed bedroom, dressing room and elegant ensuite bathroom. There are two further ensuite bedrooms, two additional bedrooms and a spacious family bathroom, all finished to the same exacting standard found throughout the home.\n\nOffering a seamless blend of architectural heritage and contemporary luxury, Annacrivey is a truly exceptional family home where every detail has been considered and every space expertly crafted."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nSpeckled polished terrazzo flooring bound by a rich emerald border and traced with hairline brass reflects light. Door to cloaks closet.\n\nLiving Room - \nCrittal wall with doors open to the living room. Chevron, dark grey Trunk flooring. White marble, art deco, open fireplace. Wall to wall windows with French doors to the patio area.\n\nDinning Room - \nChevron, dark grey Trunk flooring. Recessed mood floor lighting. Fitted sideboard.\n\nFamily Room - \nChevron, dark grey Trunk flooring. Dual aspect. French door to patio.\n\nGuest Toilet - \nTerazzo floor. Fully tiled with matt ceramic tiled flooring. Black stone oval wash hand basin. Toilet.\n\nUtility Room - \nFitted presses incorporating broom cupboard, storage presses, laundry buckets. Boiler cupboard. Plumbed for washing machine. Provision for waist level appliances. Sink unit. Window to side. Door to side.\n\nStudy - \nFitted office unit incorporating storage detail to include filing space lined with wood finish. Drawers and shelving. Storage cabinet.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - \nNoel Dempsey fitted kitchen in soft matt black offset by Buster and Punch hardware and off-white quartz worktop with soft grey veining. Well designed storage units include larder drawer with concertina door and wine cooler. Siemens induction hob with downdraft extractor fan. Black sink with Quooker tap for instant hot water. Separate larder style fridge and freezer. Coffee maker. Combi-wave and dual steamer and oven and 2 x warming drawers. Centre island providing family-friendly dining space for bar stools. Banquette seating for more formal dining. Six pillars of reeded glass bricks and a wall of ceiling high windows reflects lots of light. French door to garden.\n\nMain Bedroom - \nBright, open room with dual aspect. Gable wall incorporating a row of 6 floor to ceiling glass bricks. Large picture window to the back garden. Curved wall detail.\n\nEn-Suite - \nHis and hers basins in large white vanity unit, tiled white back wall with white hexagonal flooring. Geometric green tiling on opposite walls. Crittal shower cubicle with gold fittings to include rainbow shower head.\n\nDressing Room - \nWell appointed and cleverly designed with plenty of full and half length hanging space, drawers and shelves. Wood finish.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nLarge double overlooking the back garden. Fitted wardrobes. Steps down to\n\nEn-Suite - \nCrittal style shower cubicle with rainbow shower and shower attachment. White textured wall tiles. Dark hexagonal floor tiles. Window to the side.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nLarge double overlooking the front garden. Fitted wardrobes. Steps down to\n\nEn-Suite - \nCrittal style shower cubicle with rainbow shower and shower attachment. White textured wall tiles. Dark hexagonal floor tiles. Window to the side.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes, built-in desk unit and separate vanity unit.\n\nBedroom 5 - \nDouble bedroom to the front. Fitted wardrobes. Access to roof.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nLarge family bathroom. Twin basin in large vanity unit. Crittal style shower unit, honeycomb ceramic tiled flooring in white. Contemporary oval free standing bath. Toilet with back to wall pan. Window to the front.\n\nGym - \nLarge gym with rubber tiled flooring for maximum shock absorption. Mirror with strip lighting. Sauna with terrazzo style tiling and seating.\n\nLarge Storage Room - \nWith electricity and provision for additional white goods if required.\n\nPatio Area - \nPositioned to enjoy the setting sun. Outdoor tap.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Refurbished to impeccable standards with high end finishes</li><li>Design by Kruger Lyons Architects</li><li>Extending to 283sqm/3,046sqft approx with an additional 51sqm/552sqft approx in the detached gym and separate storage room. </li><li>Chevron flooring and doors with hidden hinges supplied by Trunk Floor</li><li>Terazzo flooring and finishes by P.J. Ryan Terrazzo and Mosaic Specialists</li><li>Noel Dempsey fitted kitchen with integrated Siemens appliances</li><li>Kitchen handles by Buster and Punch</li><li>Quartz kitchen countertops and splashbacks from The Stone Gallery</li><li>Bathroom sanitary ware by Lusso Stone</li><li>Light controls in the kitchen and living room by Rako Lighting</li><li>System line built-in speakers in the kitchen, sitting room, study and main bedroom</li><li>18 solar panels installed in January 2024</li><li>Air to Water heat pump</li><li>Mechanical ventilation with heat recovery</li><li>*Sizes are approximate</ul>"
      },
